    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `buffer_only` mode, a storage prefetch can be cancelled and reissued with the same `CacheRequestHandle` while the original query is still in flight. The hit-queue drain looks up the current prefetch by handle, so processing the terminated old operation revokes the replacement and removes its prefix context. The same problem occurs when an old hit remains queued for allocation after cancellation.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Require `info.operation is operation` before updating the current prefetch from a query result or retrying a queued allocation. Storage-belief updates still run when consuming the synchronized query result, before this check.\n- Add regressions for late misses, late hits, and queued hits consumed after cancellation and reissue. Check that the replacement and its prefix context survive, and that its own query result is still processed.\n\n## Verification\n\nCPU unit tests on two Linux hosts, each using Python 3.11 and PyTorch 2.10.0+cpu:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python SGLANG_USE_CPU_ENGINE=0 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \\\n  python -m pytest -q \\\n  test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_storage_prefetch_lifecycle.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_buffer_mode_sidecar.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_hicache_pp_sync_drain.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_pp_prefetch_ticket.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_unified_hicache_transfer_lifecycle.py\n```\n\nBoth hosts: **41 passed, 22 subtests passed**. Running the new regressions with `UnifiedRadixCache` from `dfc89580f1225d2806f7d60ed105761cc5aff067` fails in all three scenarios: the replacement has been removed from `ongoing_prefetch`.\n\nThe new tests use fixture-backed cache state and the actual prefetch lifecycle methods. No model inference or accelerator transfer was exercised.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with the repository's pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] Add regression tests to the registered CPU unit suite.\n- [x] Follow the repository's code style.\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my own code.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38868902605](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38868902605)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38868902487](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38868902487)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38868902562](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38868902562)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
